# The Lockheed Martin F-35B Lightning II, one F135-PW-600: a flight model
# written for glideslope from what is published of it - its size, weights and
# engine, and its maximum Mach and range (assets/figures/f35b.xml) - by
# tools/make_f35b.py. The F-35B is a STOVL aeroplane: her lift fan, roll posts
# and swivelling nozzle are modelled, and the hover control law hovers and
# lands her vertically; the AI still takes her off and lands her on a runway
# like any other fighter, and her short take-off, flown in a figure, is longer
# than her requirement's.
#
#   name TEXT...                 what it is called
#   model NAME                   its JSBSim model, in data/jsbsim/aircraft
#   start AIRSPEED_KT THROTTLE   a flight begun in the air: its calibrated
#                                airspeed, and the throttle that holds it
#
# Its published figures, if it has them, are data/figures/MODEL.xml, and its
# selftest's log data/selftest/MODEL.log (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).

name Lockheed Martin F-35B Lightning II
model f35b
class fighter
start 300 0.47
# Her main tyres and brakes, for a wet runway's grip (docs/ASSETS.md):
# An ESTIMATE: neither her tyre nor its pressure is published; 300 psi, by
# the F-15's 305 and the F-22's 286. Her anti-skid, fully modulating, is an
# estimate too (Hydro-Aire's Mark V was on the X-35).
brakes 300 fully-modulating
# Her gear-extended speed, VLE, knots (src/sim/catalogue.hpp): NOT PUBLISHED: no figure was found, her flight manual being not public.
# 250 kt stands in, the F-15C's and the lowest of the jets' published limits.
gear-extended 250
